            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Taiwanese Mahjong is a four-player regional Mahjong variant known for local table conventions and expanded tactical tempo compared with some other forms. It keeps classic draw-discard meld structure and fan-based outcome evaluation.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Taiwanese table practice evolved from broader Chinese Mahjong traditions with region-specific handling of flow, value, and hand-development tempo.',
              },
